(1687765, 225813, 36328, '<td valign="top">Really nice image. IMHO I would crop this in portrait, losing the the right half of the picture, making it less about the landscape and more about the tree trunks in the water....which ever way you crop it though, this photo would really benefit from using the crop tool to straighten the horizon. Contact me it you need to know how. Give it a strong 9. Good luck! IJM</td>', 'Really nice image. IMHO I would crop this in portrait, losing the the right half of the picture, making it less about the landscape and more about the tree trunks in the water....which ever way you crop it though, this photo would really benefit from using the crop tool to straighten the horizon. Contact me it you need to know how. Give it a strong 9. Good luck! IJM', '2005-09-08 18:40:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1687769, 228221, 36328, '<td valign="top">One of the best ''tree branch'' entries. I love the negitive space in this compisition. Take the original and crop it using panaramic dimenisons to see what it looks like. Anyway, strong 9 and tonnes of luck. IJM</td>', 'One of the best ''tree branch'' entries. I love the negitive space in this compisition. Take the original and crop it using panaramic dimenisons to see what it looks like. Anyway, strong 9 and tonnes of luck. IJM', '2005-09-08 18:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
