(1694094, 227672, 4514, '<td valign="top">Well I would say this shot leaves me with a petrified feeling.<br/>You managed to fill the frame here and in my honest oppinion, I believe you have filled it too much.  At the same time you leave the eye wandering for a Focal point.<br/>Do not get me wrong,  your contrast on this shot is very nice along with a nice sharp focus.  It really is difficult to give a very in depth critique without knowing the Camera used or the settings.  With that I will say that personally I would have backed out a tad.  I am wondering what is on either side of this rock.  I would assume other rocks.  <br/> <br/>John</td>', 'Well I would say this shot leaves me with a petrified feeling.You managed to fill the frame here and in my honest oppinion, I believe you have filled it too much.  At the same time you leave the eye wandering for a Focal point.Do not get me wrong,  your contrast on this shot is very nice along with a nice sharp focus.  It really is difficult to give a very in depth critique without knowing the Camera used or the settings.  With that I will say that personally I would have backed out a tad.  I am wondering what is on either side of this rock.  I would assume other rocks.   John', '2005-09-11 00:37:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1694098, 227918, 42984, '<td valign="top">That''s a pretty wow whale shot, struggling to score well as  "branch" i think, which is a pity</td>', 'That''s a pretty wow whale shot, struggling to score well as  "branch" i think, which is a pity', '2005-09-11 00:39:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1694110, 226124, 4514, '<td valign="top">This almost looks like a palm tree.  With that being said,  I will have to say you have a rather intresting shot here.  Not sure if I like this particular subject matter, but interpretation is 9/10ths the law.  I understand how hard this must have been to try to control the dust on this peice of Mirror or what ever you used.  <br/>I think the persective is good here but I think the composition lacks and when I say that the Joining should be the true focal point.  I would want to see just a tad bit more then what you show on the top "branches"  Of course I was not there.  I do not know what is right outside the frame of view.  I think this is an intresting shot.  Did you try car wax or Rain X.   I believe that water would have beaded better.  Plus wax would help with dust removal.  Intresting lighting from rear/above.   Well time to go.  <br/>Have fun.<br/> <br/>John</td>', 'This almost looks like a palm tree.  With that being said,  I will have to say you have a rather intresting shot here.  Not sure if I like this particular subject matter, but interpretation is 9/10ths the law.  I understand how hard this must have been to try to control the dust on this peice of Mirror or what ever you used.  I think the persective is good here but I think the composition lacks and when I say that the Joining should be the true focal point.  I would want to see just a tad bit more then what you show on the top "branches"  Of course I was not there.  I do not know what is right outside the frame of view.  I think this is an intresting shot.  Did you try car wax or Rain X.   I believe that water would have beaded better.  Plus wax would help with dust removal.  Intresting lighting from rear/above.   Well time to go.  Have fun. John', '2005-09-11 00:44:54.000000', NULL, 1),
